1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Your car dies at stoplights —

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
and it's not the battery.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Idle feels rough,

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
or the RPM bounces up and down while you're stopped.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
One clue: a dirty idle air control valve.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
It manages airflow when your foot's off the gas.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
When it gets clogged with carbon,

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
idle gets unstable — sometimes enough to stall.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Don't just replace the battery and hope.

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
Get the idle system checked.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before it strands you at a light.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
